<title>MALTA: PRESS DIGEST - Malta - Sept 10.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Malta - Sept 10.</headline>
<dateline>VALLETTA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the leading stories in the Maltese press on Tuesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>THE TIMES</p>
<p>- Malta enthusiastic for single European currency.</p>
<p>- Minister rebuts opposition Labour Party claims on commitment to fight drugs. Home Affaires Minister Tonio Borg says 514 drug-related arrests were made so far this year.</p>
<p>IN-NAZZJON</p>
<p>- Government against legalising drugs.</p>
<p>L-ORIZZONT</p>
<p>- Opposition finance spokesman Lino Spiteri says Labour Party, once elected, will not introduce new taxes to replace VAT.</p>
</text>
